msgctxt "#32102"
msgid "Smaller steps give a closer picture and more frames to make."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32103"
msgid "About 20 seconds after a film starts, frames around the current position are made in the background, so the preview is instant. Off: a frame is made only when you seek to it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32104"
msgid "On Linux boxes the frames stay in /tmp (memory) and nothing is written to the storage. Off: the frames of the last 3 films are kept in Kodi's temp folder."
msgstr ""

